title: Reconstruction Fatigue
tags: event
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: reconstructionPlanActive = 1 and year = 1872 and month = 3 and (VA_admitted = 0 or NC_admitted = 0 or SC_admitted = 0 or GA_admitted = 0 or AL_admitted = 0 or FL_admitted = 0 or MS_admitted = 0 or AR_admitted = 0 or TX_admitted = 0 or LA_admitted = 0)
on-arrival: {!
    Q.fatigue_readmit_list = "";
    let stateNames = {
        VA: "Virginia", NC: "North Carolina", SC: "South Carolina", GA: "Georgia",
        AL: "Alabama", FL: "Florida", MS: "Mississippi", AK: "Arkansas",
        TX: "Texas", LA: "Louisiana"
    };

    for (let state of Q.southern_states) {
        if (Q[state + "_admitted"] == 0) {
            if (Q.fatigue_readmit_list.length > 0) Q.fatigue_readmit_list += ", ";
            Q.fatigue_readmit_list += stateNames[state];
        }
    }
!}

= The Public Tires of Reconstruction

A decade of occupation, military tribunals, and federal oversight has worn down Northern patience. Newspapers North and South increasingly call Reconstruction a failed, endless project, and even sympathetic Republicans admit the public no longer has the stomach to hold the remaining Southern states outside the Union indefinitely.

Still outside Congress: [+ fatigue_readmit_list +].

Do you let public pressure force the issue and clear these states for readmission regardless of where their Reconstruction Score currently stands?

- @force_readmit: Yield to the pressure — clear the remaining states for readmission.
- @refuse_readmit: Hold the line — keep Reconstruction's conditions in place, popularity be damned.

@force_readmit
on-arrival: {!
    for (let state of Q.southern_states) {
        if (Q[state + "_admitted"] == 0) {
            Q[state + "_canReadmit"] = 1;
        }
    }
!}

Congress moves to formally clear the way for readmission, whatever the lingering conditions. It is a practical concession to public fatigue — and a quiet admission that Reconstruction's aims will go unfinished in [+ fatigue_readmit_list +].

@refuse_readmit
on-arrival: {!
    reconstruction_support -= 15;
    radical_dissent -= 3;
    conservative_strength += 5;
    conservative_dissent -= 2;
!}

You hold firm. [+ fatigue_readmit_list +] will remain outside Congress until they meet the conditions laid out under Reconstruction — no matter how loudly the public clamors for an end to it. It is a deeply unpopular stand, but a principled one.